  <layout>One printed page, text only, no margin notes. Top: continuation of a poem in italic verse, ending with the signature "I. I. B." at right. Below a double rule: title block centred (DE CVLICE GLOBVLO, subtitle, CARMEN), then "Ad I. Baptistam Rothanum.", then the poem in italic verse. Signature "G. j" at lower right, below the text.</layout>
  <page_number>97</page_number>
  <running_head>VARIA POEMATA</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <signature>G. j</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">
      <i>Gemellíq; senum vident ocelli.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Nunc vos luminibus meis misellis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>Certam fertis opem benigniora</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>Vestris lucidulis specilla flammis.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Sic Phoebi, Charitum, &amp; nouem sororum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Interesse mihi licet Choreis.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Sic clara licet eruditione</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Semper voluere nobiles libellos.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9" para="true">I. I. B.</l>
    <l n="10" type="heading" level="1" para="true">DE CVLICE GLOBVLO</l>
    <l n="11" type="heading" level="1">Succino, siue Electro</l>
    <l n="12" type="heading" level="1">includo, CARMEN,</l>
    <l n="13" type="heading" level="2" para="true">
      <i>Ad I. Baptistam Rothanum.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14" para="true">
      <i>SI tecum mihi nunc licet iocari,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Et nugas dare nobiles amico,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Salésq; innocuos, facetiásq;:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Defuncti Culicis, Rothane, Manes</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Mitto pallidulos minutulósque.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Rides? Limpidula videre fas est</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Iamiam (ni tibi lippiant ocelli)</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>Illos molliter vrnula iacentes:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Annosam nec opus tibi Sibillam</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Signature "G. j" is partly faint; the final letter may be a superscript or a mark, read as "j" with [?] doubt. The opening word of the poem is an italic capital S with a large initial; read as printed. The line "Gemellíq; senum vident ocelli." is partly worn; "senum" is read with some doubt.</notes>
</page>
